{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/124996-statue-stolen-from-neopagan-temple-in-nevada-during-easter","id":124996,"title":"Statue Stolen From Neopagan Temple In Nevada During Easter","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-03T22:25:39-07:00","id":124996,"title":"Statue Stolen From Neopagan Temple In Nevada During Easter","content":"For once, Shock isn't the one reporting in. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Source: <a href=\"http://www.jrn.com/ktnv/news/you-ask-we-investigate/Missing-statue-a-mystery-for-Cactus-Springs-temple-256104831.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.jrn.com/ktnv/news/you-ask...256104831.html</a><br /> <br /> <b>Cactus Springs, NV (KTNV)</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:FrutigerLTPro-Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> --<span style=\"font-size:14px\"> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">A decades-old statue of an Egyptian goddess is missing from a temple in the middle of the Nevada desert creating a mystery for frequent visitors.</span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\">Someone removed the statue of Sekhmet from the Temple of Goddess Spirituality between Friday night and Saturday morning, said priestess Candace Ross. The statue is 21 years old, approximately five feet tall and less than 100 pounds, Ross said.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\">&quot;To walk in here and not see her was very shocking,&quot; said Ross.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\">The temple, about 45 minutes north of Las Vegas, welcomes visitors to honor and pray to goddesses in a quiet, peaceful setting. But Sekhmet is special. The temple is dedicated to her.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\">&quot;She just means a lot to people,&quot; said Ross.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\">The statue featured the goddess's lion head with a crown on a female body. The temple has open archways allowing anyone to enter at any time. Ross has placed a picture of the statue in the empty space where the goddess used to sit.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\">&quot;Initially, I was thinking it might be a teenage prank and that she would be returned in a day or two but now that that hasn't happened, I'm really not sure what's gone on,&quot; said Ross.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\">The priestess said the temple has not had major problems with crime. When Ross arrived Saturday morning, she found the statue's necklace on the drive in front of the temple and tire tracks. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\">Las Vegas Metropolitan Police are investigating the case but do not have a lot of details, said police spokesman officer Larry Hadfield. As of Monday, no arrests had been made, he said.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\">&quot;We were devastated,&quot; said temple visitor Kevin Fitzgerald of Las Vegas.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\">Fitzgerald said he and his wife married at the temple in front of the statue in 2010. He believes the act was a hate crime, but police stressed they are still looking into the case. Fitzgerald was at the temple for Earth Day.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\">&quot;Though the physical presence was gone, her spirit was there stronger than ever,&quot; Fitzgerald said.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\">Friends of the temple are offering a $2,000 reward for information leading to the arrest and conviction of whoever is responsible.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\">&quot;My fear is someone who doesn't understand what we do here has taken her and may damage the statue,&quot; Ross said.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\">The statue was created by Marsha Gomez, who died in 1998, Ross said. Replacing it will likely cost thousands of dollars. Ross said she is also considering a security system, something she had shied away from in the past to allow visitors privacy.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}